A||||9||Adrift||Headlights not working AT ALL - wiring question inside||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||12-07-2001||06:23 PM||||My headlights don't work (they never have) - i'm not refering to the motor, or anything, If I plug the actual headlight into its socket and nothing else (none of the motor stuff) I still get no response. I thought that my socket was dead(It was full of this black shiny sticky stuff) so I got a few sockets from the boneyard to replace it with. <P>The new sockets have one green, two beige and one black coming out of them<P>the old one had two green, two beige and one black. <P>I tried to wire the two green together from the old socket to the single green for the new one but this caused a short circuit (a spark came out when I plugged the battery in, so i pulled it out instantly.<P>I pulled out one of the green wires so that there was now one wire from the car not connected to anything, and I no longer got a short circuit but the wire Still didn't work. <P>I already tried a different bulb - didn't work.<P>Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Adrift||12-07-2001||09:17 PM||||BUMP||||reg||1
Z||000002||bad911||12-07-2001||11:24 PM||||OK, hit your light switch and then your high beams... does the high-beam indicator come on? If it doesn't, (and assuming the bulb is OK) then most likely your Fusible Link B is toast. Do you have a volt meter or a test light?<P>The green is your high-beam, the beige is the low and the black is ground. The left socket has two beiges and two greens: one each is from the dimmer switch and is the power supply, and the others feed the right socket which has only one of each color.<P>------------------<BR>87 2.8 AT SE<BR>85 4.9 project<p>[This message has been edited by bad911 (edited 12-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Adrift||12-08-2001||01:38 AM||||My high beam indicator Does come on - I don't have a test light, although I could quite easily go out and buy one...<P>Any other ideas? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Adrift||12-08-2001||01:46 AM||||How do I check if my fuseable link is toast? Where is my fuseable link?||||reg||1
Z||000005||bad911||12-08-2001||10:21 AM||||Since the indicator comes on your fusible link is ok and you've got power thru your headlight switch and dimmer switch. That's good!  Clean up the black stuff from the socket and the light's prongs... [had the same prob on my 87. I wasn't paying close enough attention last night, sorry.] Get the lamp's prongs to be shiney, you might have to resort to stuff like Scotchbrite and lacquer thinner but an SOS pad would eventually get you there. If the stuff is in the sockets you're using, you'll have to use a solvent and get creative. You can try to use a mini-screwdriver covered with a rag but it's easier to shave some wood splinters and dip them in lacquer thinner or gasoline and swab-out the socket's terminals. Make sure you get them clean enough that you see nice shiney metal or you'll have intermittant lights. Do your front parking lights work? That means the ground-circuit is ok.  <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||12-08-2001||10:51 AM||||The terminals in that socket should be removable. there is a usually a notch in one side of the hole where the headlamp enters.<P>that lets you release each terminal and clean it.<P>In reality you've gotten way ahead of yourself trying to splice connectors. Both lamps dead is usually not the sockets.<P>the first thing you should be doing it using an Ohm meter to check for a ground on the socket. <P>You've already seen that the fuze link is good. a working high beam indicator also says the circuit breaker inside the headlight switch is good and it's completing the circuit in the switch.<P>The "goo" in the socket is an anti corrosion agent. Once you clean the terminals pack them with dielecrtic grease.<P>tan = low<BR>lt green = high<BR>black = ground<P>The ground has two anchors, but I don't remember just where. it's entirely posible for both to have failed. does it have park/turn in front? those use the same ground anchors.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
